<p>Just to be clear, the skip loves everyone, except for those trolls obviously.<br />
If you look at the table again, you'll notice that Anthony Miles is the most frequent requestor. This, along with the types of hugs he requested and his comments were supposed to imply the condition he is currently in. The skip suposedly &quot;liked&quot; giving these hugs and surely it has noticed Anthony Miles and also possibly the condition he is in, hence why it repeatedly tried giving those hugs he previously requested.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>And why exactly has it been unable to &quot;meet&quot; demands since the Foundation attempted to &quot;kill&quot; the SCP, when the Foundation eventually restored the website?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The Foundation did not attempt to kill the SCP. They just made the website inaccesible to the civilians. As to why its hugs &quot;Failed&quot; afterward, this is another implication to the current condition Anthonyy Miles is in. The &quot;Out of Range&quot; is a really big clue to what eventually happened to Anthony.</p>
<p>I'm not going to directly explain the meaning of those &quot;Updates&quot; so that it would not conflict with other people's personal explanation for it. We know that the skip will enter a refractory period after delivering a hug. This period previously lasted for 24 to 145 hours but in the &quot;Updates&quot; it says that this period is getting shorter and shorter until it is eventually reduced to less than 24 hours. This change occurred right after that &quot;thing&quot; with Anthony Miles.</p>
<p>Now why do some things enter a refractory period or a cool down period after doing something?</p>
<p>Let's say the skip is truly a benevolent being that really liked giving those much-desired hugs. How do you think will a being of this nature respond to what happened to Anthony Miles? Surely the skip would not want something like that to happen again, would it?</p>
